Experimental Hyper-V guest integration. Enable KVP with:
    ln -s /etc/sv/hv-kvp-daemon /var/service/
    sv status hv-kvp-daemon
Enable host Data Exchange. KVP needs hv_utils and /dev/vmbus/hv_kvp.
DHCP reporting is an observed dynamic IPv4 heuristic. DNS reads resolv.conf.
Host IP injection fails closed. VSS is optional and requires disposable-VM
freeze/thaw testing before enabling. File copy binary is included without a
service; UIO binding and behavior are untested. lsvmbus is a separate Python
subpackage. No services are enabled automatically.
Only x86_64 glibc is supported. Runtime acceptance on Hyper-V is pending.
